 "about_text": "Yiwei Gallery was founded in Los Angeles in 2019 by curator and collector Yiwei Lu, initially operating an artist-in-residence program out of a house before formally opening in Venice Beach in 2021. The gallery has focused on cultural exchange, consistently centering artists from East Asia and its diaspora alongside American and European artists working in painting, installation, textile and photography. After closing its Venice Beach space in 2024, Yiwei Gallery opened a 5,000-square-foot venue in Wuhan the same year, with a new Los Angeles location planned for 2025. The gallery also co-presents the C Art Festival in Wuhan and participates widely in international art fairs.",
